    <string name="tombstone_param_scene_title">About scene</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_scene_body">The scene value identifies different system states such as screen on, screen off, night mode, or charging.
It is normally predefined by the system and should not be modified unless you understand its purpose.

Incorrect values may cause the policy to malfunction.</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_mask_title">About mask</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_mask_body">The mask is a bitmask that controls which policy rules are enabled.
Its meaning may vary across ROM versions and is often represented as a binary or numeric combination.

It is recommended to keep the default value unless you know what you are doing.</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_quota_title">About quota</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_quota_body">Quota represents a threshold or limit that may influence how often background freezing is triggered.

Higher values may reduce restriction frequency,
while lower values may make apps more likely to be limited.</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_bgmode_title">About bgMode</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_bgmode_body">bgMode indicates the background policy mode used by the system.
The exact meaning depends on internal ROM implementation.

Changing it may affect background survival or battery consumption.</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_fgsexempt_title">About fgsExempt</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_fgsexempt_body">fgsExempt controls whether foreground service processes receive additional exemptions.

Enabling it may improve background persistence,
but could also increase battery usage.</string>
    <string name="tombstone_param_risk_notice">⚠ Modifying these parameters may cause abnormal behavior or increased battery usage. Proceed at your own risk.</string>
